    "title": "What fast food restaurants are open and closed on Easter? McDonald's, Wendy's, more",
    "text": "April 18, 2025Updated April 20, 2025, 12:05 a.m. ETEaster, a Christian holiday commemorating the resurrection of Jesus Christ, lands this Sunday, marking the end of the 40-day Lent season, a time of prayer, fasting and giving.Restaurants that already close on Sundays, such as Chick-Fil-A, are closed on Easter. But for those looking to celebrate the end of Lent with some fast food, there are plenty of other quick service and dine-in restaurants that stay open.Here’s a list of some drive-thru restaurants, coffee shops, quick service and sit-down restaurants that were either open last year or confirmed to USA TODAY that they will be open for Easter 2025.Hours may vary by location, so it's always a good idea to call and double-check whether the restaurant you'd like to eat at is open and/or doesn't have modified hours.When is Easter 2025?Easter this year lands on Sunday, April 20.Fast food restaurants open on Easter SundayMcDonald'sWendy’sTaco BellBurger KingDairy QueenCoffee shops open on Easter SundayStarbucksDunkin'Chain restaurants open on Easter SundayCracker BarrelGolden CorralApplebee’sIHOPCheesecake FactoryChili’sBuffalo Wild WingsP.F. Chang’sPanera BreadWhat grocery stores will be open and closed on Easter Sunday?Aldi: ClosedCostco: ClosedIkea: Open from 10 a.m. to 6 p.m.Jungle Jim's: Open 8 a.m. to 8 p.m.Kroger: Most stores will be openMeijer: Open from 8 a.m. to 5 p.m.Sam's Club: ClosedTarget: ClosedTrader Joe's: Stores open regular hoursWalmart: Stores open regular hoursWhole Foods: Most stores are open, but hours may vary",
